        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Leafs are being rebuilt from the inside out, and that is the first honest bit of optimism this franchise has had in a while. <strong>Tyler Hopkins' invitation to Team Canada camp</strong> is the kind of prospect signal Toronto has craved - real traction, not just wishful talk. After finishing 78 points and 8th in the Atlantic Division, the club is clearly in roster surgery mode, not wallpapering over problems. The Duhaime signing has already sharpened the debate around Steven Lorentz's place, while the Domi fit remains a neat little gamble because the forward mix still needs edge and finish. Meanwhile, the Marner camp's public frustration only hardens the sense that change was inevitable. <strong>What matters now is whether Toronto turns prospect buzz and cap arithmetic into a cleaner, faster lineup before camp opens.</strong>",
