      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Blue Jays finally found a clean, emphatic night - and they needed it. <strong>Dylan Cease carved up Boston with a one-hit complete game in Toronto's 6-0 win Saturday</strong>, a performance that snapped the kind of foggy, uneven stretch that has left this club at 48-57, fifth in the AL East and still buried 13.5 games back. Cease was the story, but George Springer supplied the thunder with a three-run homer in a five-run third, the sort of burst this lineup has too rarely delivered. That is the split-screen reality of this season: flashes of life, then too many dead stretches. <strong>Next comes another date with the Red Sox on Sunday afternoon in Boston</strong> - and the Blue Jays need the arm and the bite to travel.",
        "updated": "Updated July 26, 2026"
      },
