      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The summer market keeps tugging at Toronto with one hand and poking holes in the roster with the other - and that is the whole story now. <strong>Kyle Anderson has agreed to a one-year, $3.9 million deal, while Toronto is also set to keep Trace Jackson-Davis on a $2.4 million team option</strong>, the kind of tidy, practical business that suggests a front office still prefers depth over drama. With no games ahead and the season finished, the Raptors sit 3rd in the Atlantic Division, a reminder of where they landed before the real work began. The louder noise is elsewhere: the DeMar DeRozan chatter never really dies, and the Kawhi Leonard investigation story hangs over every rumor like weather. But this team needs bodies and fit, not nostalgia. <strong>Watch whether Toronto uses its remaining flexibility on another wing or spends the last two-way spot on Seth Lundy</strong>.",
